{
  "audio": "006.this-is-also.mp3",
  "paragraph": 6,
  "text": "This is also why a harness is very different from the heavy agent frameworks that were popular a couple of years ago. Rigid frameworks try to hardcode intelligence into fixed prompt chains, brittle multi-agent graphs, and fragile regex parsers. Every time a stronger model ships, that scaffolding gets in the way and breaks. Modern harnesses like Claude Code, OpenCode, and Aider follow the bitter lesson instead: give the model a minimal set of Unix-like primitives, shell, files, search, and verification, and let the model drive.",
